The repo convention is focused per-class test files with a small local harness (e.g. `doctor_command_test.dart` has its own `_tmp`, `_writeEnv` helper, and per-concern functions). Splitting the alias-routing tests into `test/cli_dispatcher_alias_test.dart` fits the established pattern perfectly: small harness, `_writeEnv`-style helper, focused groups. Zero churn on existing tests.

Plan:
1. Remove `_testAliasRouting` + `_testAliasRoutingFileTier` + `_dispatchTool` from `cli_dispatcher_test.dart` and their main() registrations → file back to 791 lines.
2. Create `test/cli_dispatcher_alias_test.dart` (~100 lines) with the harness + the 5 tests + helper.

The new file harness needs the same isolation setup:
```dart
void main() {
  setUpAll(() => PropertyReader.testIsolation = true);
  tearDownAll(() {
    PropertyReader.testIsolation = false;
    PropertyReader.testEnvironment.clear();
  });
  setUp(() {
    _tmp = Directory.systemTemp.createTempSync('dmtools_cli_alias_');
    PropertyReader.setOverrides({});
    PropertyReader.testEnvironment.clear();
    _lines = [];
    _dispatcher = CliDispatcher(
      writer: _lines.add,
      propertyReader: PropertyReader(basePath: _tmp.path),
      isTty: () => false,
    );
  });
  tearDown(() {
    PropertyReader.clearOverrides();
    if (_tmp.existsSync()) _tmp.deleteSync(recursive: true);
  });
  ...
}
```

With `testEnvironment.clear()` in setUp, no per-group setUp needed.

Also: `_dispatchTool(args, {int code = 1})` — assert code, return decoded. Note `dart test` runs each test FILE in its own isolate — no interference with cli_dispatcher_test.dart's globals.

Public docs gate: test files are in `sources: [lib, bin, test]` for coverage; the public_docs gate checks lib public API presumably. Test functions are private (underscore), no doc requirements beyond what I add.

Write the new file.

